# Remotler control plane — automatic HTTPS + WSS reverse proxy in front of the Node server.
# Caddy fetches/renews a Let's Encrypt certificate for the domain automatically and
# transparently proxies WebSocket upgrades, so the app connects over wss:// on 443.
#
# 1. Point an A record (e.g. remotler.com) at the droplet's public IP.
# 2. Replace the domain below and email.
# 3. Put this at /etc/caddy/Caddyfile and: sudo systemctl reload caddy
#
# The Node server keeps listening on 127.0.0.1:8081 (not exposed publicly).

{
	email admin@remotler.com
}

remotler.com {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8081
}
